            <ArticleTitle>A successfully treated case of blunt traumatic right coronary ostium rupture.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1001-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cardiac tamponade due to coronary artery rupture, as a consequence of blunt trauma, is a rare but usually fatal condition. We successfully obtained primary hemostasis with emergency room thoracotomy, followed by delayed definitive treatment of the ruptured right coronary artery ostium in a motor vehicle accident victim with multifocal hemorrhagic lesions. Survival of patients with the described serious trauma has not been reported, and we discuss herein our treatment strategy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
